rules:
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Workflows must adhere to the CAS Workflow Execution Model, maintaining
    separation between orchestration (Runner), reasoning (Workflow), and knowledge
    access (Providers), and must not assume repository structures.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maintains consistent interpretation between pattern maturity and decision
    lifecycle, ensuring that knowledge evolution and governance status are not conflated.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All new patterns must be created as supporting by default to ensure they
    are validated through usage and evidence before being considered for core status.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Prohibits the consolidation of patterns across different architectural
    layers to maintain separation between governance, execution, contracts, and reliability
    concerns.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Pattern promotion to core architecture must be supported by strong evidence
    from multiple sources or systems to ensure stability.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work is the authoritative source for architectural planning;
    all generated artifacts must derive status from it to avoid state divergence.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All architectural decisions must be expressed using the structured YAML
    decision schema (ADR) to enable machine processing and consistent rendering.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must utilize the shared Knowledge Workspace and are prohibited
    from duplicating global governance structures like runtime/ or templates/.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Foundational contract defining semantic alignment between intent (AID),
    decisions (ADR), and system state (AEM), ensuring clear lifecycle terminology.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All heuristic-derived patterns must be grounded in observed behavior by
    including at least one linked signal as evidence.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Defines the mandatory resolution hierarchy for rule conflicts: Global
    Rules override Project Rules, which override Prompt Rules.'
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maintains human-in-the-loop control by requiring that all system-proposed
    architectural decisions be explicitly validated by an architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts act as summaries only; authoritative information
    must reside in durable source artifacts to prevent state loss during regeneration.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The ADR is the single source of truth for architectural decisions; metadata
    and AEM maps must be derived solely from ADR records.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines mandatory criteria (Recurrence, Impact, Reusability, Stability)
    and evidence requirements for promoting a candidate signal to a pattern.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Decisions must be persisted as structured ADR files before they can be
    reflected in the Architecture Evolution Map (AEM) or other artifacts.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Lifecycle stages in architecture maps must be derived from decision status;
    items cannot be marked as DONE unless status is 'accepted'.
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The Architecture Evolution Map must accurately reflect and never contradict
    the states and decisions recorded in Architecture Decision Records.
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Core patterns are restricted to foundational architectural primitives;
    context-specific strategies or implementations must not be promoted to core.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
